Found while working karr #113. Pre-existing drift, not caused by it, and in a
file that lane could not touch (karr #117 was working in lib/File/SOPS.pm).

lib/File/SOPS.pm, in the "A YAML literal that overflows a double comes back as
a string" section, says of the twelve %GO_CONSTANT spellings:

    ... an ENCRYPTED one of those decrypts to a real Inf here as it always
    did, while an UNENCRYPTED one still fails verification, which is a
    separate defect and open as karr #105

karr #105 is closed and ADR 0026 shipped in the same unreleased cycle: an
unencrypted plain .inf now READS, as the float go-yaml resolves, carrying the
document token. And since karr #113 / ADR 0031 it is written back as well, so
the sentence is wrong twice over.

Same paragraph, one line up, is still correct and should stay: a literal that
overflows a double (1e400) reaches the tree as a BARE non-finite double, which
assert_representable still refuses on every write path.

Two more places in that file to check while there: the =head3 "A YAML literal
that overflows a double comes back as a string" and the extract POD around
"Since 0.003 a non-finite YAML literal comes back from an unencrypted slot as
a string" -- both are about ADR 0023 literals and read correct, but they sit
next to the wrong sentence and a reader will not separate them.

Documentation only, no behaviour. API lane (lib/File/SOPS.pm POD).
ERLEDIGT 2026-08-21 in ed827d5 (karr #123), ohne eigenen Durchgang. Die Lane hat beim Ergaenzen der edit-POD den ganzen Abschnitt durchgesehen und die veraltete Behauptung mitkorrigiert -- 'an UNENCRYPTED one still fails verification, which is a separate defect and open as karr #105'. Verifiziert: der Satz existiert in lib/File/SOPS.pm nicht mehr. Das ist der richtige Weg fuer eine Stelle wie diese: wer ohnehin in der Datei steht und den Abschnitt liest, korrigiert ihn, statt ein zweites Ticket abzuwarten.
